return
RHASH_AR_TABLE_MAX_BOUND
;
}
As you may be able to see, it’s essentially a linear, AKA
O(n)
, search.
We receive the
hint
of the key we’re searching for, and linearly search for a match in the table list.
When a match is found, since we have to worry about collisions, we invoke
Object#eql?
(
ar_equal
), and if it returns false,
we continue our search until we reach the end of the array.
